\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Abstract}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum
\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Deepfake technology facilitates the alteration of a person\u8217 s facial features in videos or images, frequently employed for non-consensual pornographic material disseminated on social media platforms. Individuals affected by deepfake pornography in Indonesia encounter significant obstacles in asserting their right to be forgotten, as specified in the Law on Sexual Violence Crimes. These challenges stem from a lack of implementing regulations, inadequate legal frameworks, and law enforcement practices that do not adequately consider gender issues. The absence of regulatory frameworks and the prevalent misuse of AI technology have resulted in a notable increase in incidents, with platforms such as Telegram emerging as key areas for disseminating altered content. Victims experience significant psychological, social, and economic repercussions. Although organizations such as the National Commission on Violence Against Women assist, there are still legal barriers that persist. In order to safeguard victims and implement the Right to Be Forgotten, Indonesia needs to tackle various legal, cultural, and enforcement obstacles, especially the insufficient gender sensitivity within law enforcement and the ambiguity surrounding relevant laws. A joint initiative involving both government and society is essential to protect victims' rights and address the increasing prevalence of deepfake pornography.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Introduction}{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 In the contemporary era of unparalleled technological progress, technology has become integral to human existence [1, 2]. In light of the Fourth Industrial Revolution, also known as Industry 4.0, the world has gained the ability to produce nearly anything due to its vast technical progress [3, 4]. Artificial Intelligence (AI) is one of the critical technologies facilitating this progression [5, 6]. The exponential advancement of technology in terms of artificial intelligence complexity has thrust humanity into a period of technological upheaval [7]. Disruption, in the context of online-based digital technology, is defined by swift, extensive, profound, systematic, and markedly distinct changes compared to the preceding paradigm. One consequence of technological disruption is the occurrence of electronic-based violence, namely electronic-based sexual violence [8, 9]. This encompasses the distribution of non-consensual intimate material or non-consensual intimate images violence, more often referred to as revenge porn and sextortion. Cybersexual violence, in a broad sense, can impact individuals of all genders. However, when examined via a gender lens, women are seen as more susceptible to becoming victims, as evidenced by the fact that 71% of incidents involve female victims [10].}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Historically, non-consensual intimate image violence was carried out by using traditional methods, specifically by disseminating content that was initially genuine documents [11]. Thus, historically, the prevention of revenge porn and sextortion was far more feasible [12, 13]. Nevertheless, the prevalence of AI, readily available to a considerable number of individuals, has heightened the alarming nature of electronic sexual crimes beyond our initial expectations. This is because it is no longer necessary to have access to the victim\u8217 s personal information; instead, a mere photograph of their face can suffice to convert it into explicit material utilizing deepfake technology, now known as deepfake pornography [14, 15].}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 The rising prevalence of sexual violence, particularly in cases of electronic-based sexual violence, such as non-consensual intimate image violence, indicates the necessity for legal safeguards to protect society from such abuse [16, 17]. The concept of non-consensual intimate image violence is intricately linked to digital traces that pose a significant risk to the dignity and reputation of victims [11, 18]. Hence, the government should ensure the realization of the right to be forgotten (RtBF) for those who have experienced electronic-based sexual violence. RtBF was initially introduced as a fundamental entitlement in the European Union [19, 20]. This entitlement grants individuals the ability to delete their data from the internet, mainly through the General Data Protection Regulation 2016/679 [21]. Although the General Data Protection Regulation exclusively applies to the European Union, other countries, including Indonesia, have embraced its principles. Within the framework of electronic-based sexual violence, the RtBF is already addressed in Article 70, Paragraph (2) letter l of Law No. 12 of 2022 on Sexual Violence Crimes (The Law on Sexual Violence Crimes). This provision ensures that victims of electronic-based sexual violence are entitled to the right to remove sexually explicit material both before and during the legal proceedings. This right implicitly embodies the expression of RtBF [9].}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 While legally mandated, implementing the RtBF encounters numerous challenges due to various circumstances, both at the governmental and societal levels. This research aims to address the author\u8217 s concerns regarding the alarming and harmful nature of deepfake pornography, as well as the lack of specific laws governing the use of AI. The goal is to provide valuable insights for future government research and policy development, particularly in implementing the RtBF for victims of deepfake pornography.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 The present study utilizes multiple theories in order to enhance the author\u8217 s analysis. First among the theories is feminist legal theory. Sarah Gamble [22] defines [feminism] is the belief that women, purely and simply because they are women, are treated inequitably within a society which is organized to prioritize male viewpoints and concerns. Within this patriarchal paradigm, women become everything men are not (or do not want to be seen to be): where men are regarded as strong, women are weak; where men are rational, they are emotional; where men are active, they are passive; and so on.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Feminist legal theory posits that the current laws are insufficient in attaining appropriate justice for women. This hypothesis is employed due to the disproportionate impact of sexual assault on women, and the policies commonly employed to handle cases of sexual violence tend to expose female victims to a high degree of vulnerability, either through criminalization or the recurrence of victimization. Within the framework of electronic-based sexual violence, several law enforcement personnel remain hesitant to utilize the Electronic Information and Transactions Law or the Pornography Law. In these cases, victims are at a significant risk of being directly confronted by the perpetrators or even being falsely identified as pornography offenders.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Within the subchapter of discussion, the author employs Lawrence Meir Friedman\u8217 s legal system theory to examine the likelihood of achieving restorative justice for victims of deepfake pornography in Indonesia. In his book \u8220 The Legal System: A Social Science Perspective,\u8221  Friedman [23] contends that the legal system must be seen as a cohesive entity comprising three distinct subsystems: legal structure, legal substance, and legal culture. This theory is employed to evaluate the actual circumstances of these three subsystems in Indonesia about achieving RtBF while developing specific and appropriate recommendations for Indonesia.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 The purpose of this study is to investigate the effects of deepfake pornography on victims, the mechanisms of victim care by service providers in Indonesia, and the potential for achieving RtBF for victims of deepfake pornography. Prior studies on RtBF primarily relied on regulations that are only partially relevant, particularly the Electronic Information and Transactions Law, the Personal Data Protection Law, and The Law on Sexual Violence Crimes, without doing a thorough analysis of the problem.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 The Emergence and Impact of Feminist Legal Theory: A Path Toward Justice for Women}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260
\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Before formally introducing the term feminist legal theory, feminism has existed since the eighteenth century. Feminism, in essence, seeks to challenge and dismantle societal structures that mistreat women simply because of their gender. Sarah Gamble [22] offers a concise definition of feminism as \u8220 the belief that women, purely and simply because they are women, are treated inequitably within a society which is organized to prioritize male viewpoints and concerns.\u8221  This definition underscores the historical and ongoing struggle women face in societies where patriarchal norms shape not only cultural and social expectations but also legal structures that marginalize their experiences and rights [24].}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Feminism itself is not a monolithic ideology. It encompasses various schools of thought, which differ in their approaches to understanding and combating gender inequality. Feminist thought can be categorized into three primary schools: liberal feminism, marxist feminism, and radical feminism. However, beyond these three, there are many other branches of feminist thought, including psychoanalytic-gender feminism, existentialist feminism, postmodern feminism, multicultural-global feminism, and ecofeminism. Each perspective offers unique insights into how gender inequality manifests and how it can be addressed in different societal contexts. For instance, liberal feminism advocates for equal rights through legal reforms, while radical feminism seeks to dismantle patriarchal structures altogether.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 A key element of feminist thought is its critique of patriarchal systems, which dominate social, political, and economic spheres and profoundly influence the construction of law. As an institution, law has historically been designed and informed by men, reflecting their experiences and priorities, often at the expense of women\u8217 s rights and perspectives. This patriarchal foundation of law perpetuates gender inequality by upholding legal norms that are not inclusive of women\u8217 s experiences and concerns. This is where feminist legal theory plays a crucial role. Feminist legal theory challenges the male-centered nature of legal systems and calls for reforming legal doctrines, institutions, and interpretations to reflect women\u8217 s experiences better and ensure gender justice.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Feminist legal theory, also known by various terms such as feminist jurisprudence, women and the law, feminist analysis of law, and gendered perspectives on law, was first introduced by Ann C. Scales [25] and in her groundbreaking article titled \u8220 Towards a Feminist Jurisprudence,\u8221  Scales emphasized the need for a feminist evaluation of legal theory and the integration of feminist thought into the legal domain. Scales argued that law, as it stood, was insufficient for addressing the unique challenges women face in patriarchal societies. She advocated for a feminist jurisprudence that would question the underlying assumptions of traditional legal theories and offer a more inclusive and equitable framework for interpreting and applying the law.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 The reality that Scales and other feminist legal theorists sought to address was that law had been historically shaped by men, for men. Legal norms and principles were created based on male experiences, with little regard for the lived realities of women. This male-dominated perspective has led to the exclusion of women's voices and experiences in the legal process, reinforcing a patriarchal culture that marginalizes women. Patricia A. Cain [26] and Martha Chamallas [27], two prominent feminist legal scholars, argued in their writings that legal reasoning cannot be considered feminist unless grounded in women\u8217 s experiences. In other words, for a legal theory to indeed be feminist, it must center on the experiences, struggles, and needs of women rather than merely adopting a gender-neutral or male-centric approach.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 At its core, feminist legal theory posits that existing legal systems are inadequate for achieving justice for women. Feminist legal theory critiques the law as an instrument that often upholds gender inequalities, whether through overt discrimination or more subtle forms of bias. Feminist legal scholars argue that the law must be reformed to protect women\u8217 s rights better, acknowledge their lived experiences, and address the unique forms of discrimination and violence they face. Feminist legal theory is not just about formally achieving equality (i.e., giving women the same rights as men) but recognizing the more profound, structural inequalities that pervade legal systems and working toward a more just and inclusive legal framework.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 One of the critical contributions of feminist legal theory is its role in evaluating and challenging existing legal norms related to women\u8217 s rights and roles in society. For example, feminist legal theory has been instrumental in highlighting the ways in which laws on sexual harassment, domestic violence, and reproductive rights have historically failed to protect women adequately. By bringing attention to these issues, feminist legal theory has spurred critical legal reforms that aim to improve the legal protections available to women. Additionally, feminist legal theory offers a framework for critiquing legal doctrines that perpetuate gender stereotypes, such as those that assume women are inherently more nurturing or less capable of making rational decisions than men.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Feminist legal theory also plays a significant role in reshaping the way we think about justice. Traditional legal systems often operate on the assumption that justice can be achieved through neutrality and objectivity. However, feminist legal scholars argue that these concepts are often illusory, as they fail to account for how gender, race, class, and other social factors shape individuals\u8217  experiences of the law. Feminist legal theory calls for a more nuanced understanding of justice that recognizes the complex interplay of power dynamics and social inequalities. By doing so, feminist legal theory seeks to create a legal system that is more responsive to the needs of marginalized groups, particularly women.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Moreover, feminist legal theory emphasizes the importance of intersectionality in legal analysis. Intersectionality, a concept first introduced by Kimberl\'e9 Crenshaw [28], refers to the ways in which different forms of discrimination (such as racism, sexism, and classism) intersect and overlap, creating unique forms of oppression. Feminist legal scholars argue that the law must take an intersectional approach to truly address the needs of all women, particularly those who face multiple forms of marginalization. For instance, laws that aim to protect women from domestic violence may be inadequate if they fail to consider the specific challenges faced by women of color, immigrant women, or women with disabilities.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 The Evolution of Gender-Based Cyber Violence: A Global and Indonesian Perspective}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260
\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Because both children and women frequently experience sexual violence, the National Commission on Violence Against Women has observed that it is essential to have an awareness of sexual violence not only from the standpoint of children\u8217 s rights but also from a more general standpoint of gender-based violence. The term \u8220 gender-based violence\u8221  refers to acts of violence that are intended at persons based on their gender and that result in physical, mental, or sexual injury, as well as threats, coercion, or other forms of deprivation of freedom [29, 30]. As a result of the proliferation of digital technology in recent years, a new type of gender-based violence has evolved. This new form of violence is known as cyber-based violence, and it has become a significant problem all over the world, especially throughout Indonesia.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 It is possible to provide a comprehensive definition of cyber-based violence, which can be described as unlawful activities that occur within cyberspace and are carried out using networks of computers or internet networks. In many cases, the victims suffer some suffering as a consequence of these crimes, whether it be financial, emotional, or psychological [31]. In 1988, the first virus was built to shut down another person\u8217 s computer. This was the first time that the concept of cyber-based violence was introduced. Since that time, the scope of cyber-based violence has broadened significantly beyond hacking and cracking to encompass more subtle kinds of online abuse. One example of this is gender-based violence committed through digital platforms, which is frequently referred to as cyber-based violence among the general public.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 The typology of cybercrime given by David Wall [32] helps us understand the various forms of violence committed online. The crimes committed against machines, the crimes committed using machines, and the crimes committed within machines are the three basic categories he uses to classify cybercrime. In computer integrity crimes, crimes against machines encompass hacking and denial of service (DoS) attacks, which are directed at computer systems. Crimes that utilize machines, often computer-assisted crimes, include some of the most common types of criminal activity, such as piracy and fraud, made easier by digital technologies. Last but not least, crimes committed within machines specifically target persons using the content that is disseminated online. These crimes include online harassment, pornography, and hate speech. This third category is mainly comprised of gender-based cyber violence, which includes practices such as harassment or the non-consensual sharing of intimate content. This type of cyber violence frequently involves the utilization of the internet to cause harm to persons, particularly women.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Several prominent instances of gender-based cyber violence have been recognized, especially in terms of specific crimes committed against individuals. As an example, one of these is harassment, which occurs when the offenders send threatening messages to their victims via email or social media in order to instill fear in them. The act of impersonation is another type of criminal activity in which thieves assume the identity of another person in order to manipulate their reputation or resources. The dissemination of pornographic material is another significant cause for concern. This occurs when websites publish explicit sexual content of both adults and children, which contributes to the sexual exploitation of those who are vulnerable. Furthermore, slander and defamation are commonplace in the digital world, with malevolent content frequently aimed at causing harm to a person's reputation or dignity.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 An increasing number of people in Indonesia are becoming concerned about gender-based cyber violence. As stated in the 2023 Annual Report of the National Commission on Violence Against Women, the form of violence that was recorded the most frequently in the public domain was cyber-based violence, with a total of 869 cases being reported. The Annual report for 2021 also reveals that there has been a significant surge in the number of instances of gender-based cyber violence, with an increase of 83% from the previous year, 2020. Considering that the internet is increasingly being used as a weapon to conduct gender-based violence, this spike is concerning since it illustrates how the internet is being exploited. Ex-boyfriends and current boyfriends were the most prevalent offenders of gender-based cyber violence in the personal sphere in 2021. The majority of cases of gender-based cyber violence in the personal sphere were related to sexual violence. In addition, a considerable number of cases occurred in the public realm, with social media friends and strangers being recognized as the primary perpetrators [33].}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 The non-consensual intimate image violence form of gender-based cyber violence has garnered international attention as one of the most disturbing kinds of cyber abuse that has been committed online. This phenomenon happens when criminals use personally identifiable or sexually explicit content, such as photographs or films, without the agreement of the victim, typically to intimidate or manipulate the victim. There are a few different names for non-consensual intimate images violence, such as revenge porn or sextortion, depending on the precise context in which it is being discussed. An ex-partner or current partner will often share intimate content without the other person\u8217 s knowledge in the context of revenge porn. This is typically done as an act of retaliation for a breakup or a perceived slight. The act of sextortion, on the other hand, is a sort of blackmail in which the perpetrator utilizes their authority or power to coerce the victim into giving sexual photographs or films, frequently under the threat of being exposed.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 The victims of these forms of cyber-based violence suffer severe psychological and emotional suffering as a result of the violence carried out online. In particular, revenge porn and sextortion are incredibly harmful since they take advantage of the victim's most private moments, so transforming intimacy into a weapon. It is common for victims to experience a sense of helplessness as they fear societal stigma, shame, or reprisal if they speak out. Once the content has been shared online, it may be practically impossible to completely erase it, which can cause long-term damage to the victim\u8217 s personal and professional life. This is because the digital nature of these crimes makes it nearly impossible to remove the content.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Given the growing number of instances of gender-based cyber violence in Indonesia, there is an immediate and pressing requirement for more robust legislative protections and support mechanisms as well as for victims. Even though Indonesia has enacted several laws to combat cybercrime, the execution of these laws continues to be a severe difficulty, particularly in disputes involving gender-based violence. In the process of pursuing justice, victims, particularly women and children, frequently encounter enormous obstacles. Many individuals are hesitant to report occurrences because they are afraid of being victimized again or do not have faith in the judicial system's capacity to protect them. This highlights the importance of increasing awareness, reforming laws, and working together with law enforcement, technology corporations, and civil society in order to address gender-based cyber abuse.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Unmasking the Threat: The Dark Reality of Deepfake Pornography and Its Impact on Society}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj
\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 At the time of its initial discovery, AI was seen as a technology that was capable of thinking in a manner similar to that of humans [34]. However, in today\u8217 s world, artificial intelligence is seen as a technology that can behave in a manner comparable to that of humans [35]. AI is distinct from robots but can be utilized to develop robots [36]. AI contains several distinctive qualities, such as the capability to be incorporated into a wide range of applications, the ability to accelerate technical breakthroughs based on the Internet of Things, and the ability to be utilized in various contexts, ranging from public services to national defense [37, 38].}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Deepfake technology is one of the technologies that has emerged as a result of the advancements in artificial intelligence [39, 40]. In 2017, a member of Reddit published a video that showed a celebrity engaging in sexually suggestive behavior [41]. This was the moment that Deepfake received widespread exposure. Deepfake content features authentic elements, can contain audio that sounds authentic and is designed to be quickly disseminated on social media platforms, all of which bring their unique issues when it comes to detecting it. Consequently, a significant number of viewers are under the impression that the video they are currently seeing is authentic [42].}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 The idea behind the phrase \u8220 deepfake\u8221  originates from the combination of the words \u8220 deep learning\u8221  and \u8220 fake\u8221 . The term \u8220 deep learning\u8221  refers to a learning process that is both deep and structured, and it uses machine learning approaches based on data representation [41, 43]. However, it is distinct from specific algorithms. An Artificial Neural Network (ANN) is the name of the layered algorithmic structure that is utilized in deep learning techniques [44]. In order to replace the face of the original subject with the face of another subject in video form, the software must be based on artificial intelligence. This is the primary characteristic of a deepfake.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Deepfakes result from Generative Adversarial Networks (GAN), a type of artificial neural network that involves two artificial neural networks working together to produce material that appears to be an authentic representation of the real thing [45]. The \u8216 generator\u8217  and the \u8216 discriminator\u8217  are the names given to these two networks, respectively [46]. The same dataset of images, videos, or audio is used to train the networks individually. It is the responsibility of the first network to generate new samples that are persuasive enough to fool the second network, which is responsible for determining whether or not the new media it sees is genuine. By going through this process, the networks are pushed to better each other. GANs can process thousands of photographs of a person and produce a new image similar to the ones that already exist without being an exact clone of the initial photograph. The amount of data required to train GANs has decreased over time, and they can now switch heads, entire bodies, and even voices. Even though deepfakes often require a large number of photos in order to generate convincing fakes, researchers have devised methods that allow them to generate fake videos using only a single photo, one example being a selfie [47].}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 As a result of the proliferation of information, rumors, and wild speculations on social media platforms, deepfakes have become a viral target. People who use social media are prone to acting rashly and readily falling for hoaxes because of the quick flow of information that they receive on these platforms. The Indonesian population is thought to be susceptible to hoaxes, which may include bogus videos. According to the Edelman Trust Barometer survey findings, nations such as Indonesia, Mexico, Argentina, and Spain are at a high risk of falling prey to misinformation, with fears ranging from 76 to 80% [48].}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 The ease with which hoax creators may win the trust of internet users drives them to continue making phony information to boost the amount of engagement they receive on social media. In addition, there is an increasing availability of deepfake software that is of high quality and hyper-realistic, and it is becoming easier to obtain. This makes it possible for users to synthesize someone\u8217 s voice, swap faces, alter expressions, and edit movies with high precision, even if they have only a limited understanding of technical abilities and no artistic expertise.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 The integration of AI with society has witnessed a notable surge in recent years. The sophisticated functionalities of this technology have merged effortlessly into daily life, providing ease and accessibility that were before inconceivable. Among the several applications of AI, one that has attracted much interest is the technology referred to as deepfake. In the creative sectors, deepfakes have transformed into a dual-edged phenomenon employed by specific individuals to damage or obliterate reputations. One very alarming abuse of deepfake technology is in the production of deepfake pornography, sometimes known as false pornography.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Deepfake pornography gained significant public attention in Indonesia following an incident involving the actress Nagita Slavina. The emergence of a 61-s pornographic video on the internet in early 2022 generated significant controversy among internet users because of its apparent inclusion of Slavina. The subsequent examination uncovered that the video resulted from deepfake manipulation, whereby the visage of Slavina was overlaid over the physical form of another person referred to as Miss Key. The authorities subsequently verified that the video's developer deliberately substituted Miss Key\u8217 s face with Slavina's, illustrating the simplicity with which deepfake technology may produce undeniably persuasive but completely falsified material.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Over the previous three years, the Annual Report of Semarang Legal Aid Institute reveals that instances of deepfake pornography are remarkably prevalent, placing among the top three most frequently reported types of sexual violence, alongside rape and domestic violence. Furthermore, corroborating this claim, Nabillah Saputri Djaelani from AwasKBGO stated that in 2023, 2% of 1,052 complaints pertained to the alteration of photos or videos for sexual purposes, commonly referred to as morphing. Djaelani emphasized that in the majority of these instances, the victims lacked any direct connection with the offenders, underscoring that anyone can be targeted by this type of digital violence as long as the offender maintains access to a photograph that can be altered into a deepfake.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 The incidence of deepfake pornography is steadily increasing, and the individuals responsible for creating such material have established what can only be characterized as international criminal networks. By June 2023, a widely circulated discussion on the social media site X, written by a user identified as @itsindahg, elevated this matter to prominence. The discussion, which has received more than 13,000 retweets, 1,200 quote tweets, 18,000 likes, and 2,400 bookmarks, indicated the presence of a Google Form being circulated online to distribute revenge pornography and non-consensual intimate images of violence, including deepfake pornography. The communication urged users to disseminate information and exert pressure on the authorities to promptly respond, as the potential victims may include any lady, regardless of location, emphasizing the indiscriminate character of this digital menace.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 The screenshots posted in the forum effectively depicted the profound level of entrenchment and organization that these actions had attained. The proliferation of non-consensual intimate images, violence, and deepfake pornography is enabled by extensive online communities, notably on platforms such as Telegram, where groups can boast over 10,000 subscribers. The content exchange process is meticulously organized, utilizing Google Forms to gather and distribute photographs and videos and the personal information of female victims, such as their complete names, Instagram URLs, and the educational institutions they are affiliated with. The presence of such extensive and well-structured collectives makes controlling the dissemination of these illegal materials exceedingly tricky. Furthermore, these communities are highly prepared to the extent that they have contingency groups readily available in case their primary group should be prohibited.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Prior to the emergence of deepfake technology, non-consensual intimate image violence victims were usually individuals who had disclosed personal photographs or films to someone they had confidence in, such as a romantic partner, only to have those materials subsequently exploited against them. Alternatively, victims were surreptitiously recorded during sexual interactions, and the footage was disseminated without their explicit agreement. During that period, non-consensual intimate image violence specifically focused on authentic, unmodified photographs and films. However, with the emergence of deepfake technology, the nature of the threat has undergone a severe transformation. Individuals who share a self-portrait on the internet are now susceptible to being targeted, as their image can be altered to produce persuasive but completely fabricated pornographic material.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 In an interview with the author, Alia Yofira Karuniana, a researcher affiliated with Purple Code Collective, voiced her apprehension about the simplicity with which deepfake technology might generate non-consensual false pornography. She emphasized that this technology is dangerous even to individuals who have never participated in exploitative conduct or disclosed personal material, as anyone might have their image altered without their awareness or agreement. This gives rise to substantial apprehensions regarding the level of readiness of the legal system and law enforcement authorities to manage technologically sophisticated criminal cases, necessitating specialized knowledge to detect and resolve.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 The dynamics between victims and perpetrators have also transformed with the widespread diffusion of deepfake technology. Historically, instances of non-consensual intimate image violence mostly applied to persons engaged in a romantic relationship, such as dating partners or spouses. Nevertheless, with the widespread availability of deepfake technology, the possible number of prospective victims has significantly increased. According to Djaelani, the majority of victims and perpetrators lack direct contact. Instead, the only requirement for producing deepfake pornography is a photograph, which can be readily acquired via social media posts. This is demonstrated by the previously mentioned Google Form, in which group members were requested to furnish the personal information of the victims they intended to \u8220 undress\u8221  using deepfake technology. The incidental usage of the term \u8220 }
{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 mau}{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0
\ulnone\cf2 \u8221  (desire) in the snapshot highlights the alarming truth that even without explicit images or videos, a wrongdoer can nonetheless digitally disrobe a victim.}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum
\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Building upon the widely circulated discussion, the author interviewed Indah Gunawan, the actual identity of the X user known as @itsindahg. Gunawan is a renowned content producer noted for her engagement with contemporary social concerns across several social media platforms such as Instagram, TikTok, YouTube, and X. Gunawan expressed his observation on the swift progress of technology during the interview, stating, \u8220 While humans are undoubtedly malevolent beings, it is the undeniable reality that technology is advancing at a rapid pace, enabling malevolent individuals to engage in more malevolent actions with greater speed and magnitude. However, the existing laws cannot keep pace with this rapid advancement\u8221 . This statement emphasizes that although technology facilitates sinister operations with greater efficiency and on a more extensive scope, the legal structures intended to safeguard against such misconduct nevertheless frequently fall behind.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Paradoxically, the widely circulated thread that Gunawan shared had positive and negative consequences for her. She documented receiving a multitude of threats in the aftermath, with the vast majority originating from males. The threats encompassed a spectrum of legal proceedings, sexual assault, and even dire threats of death. Upon contemplation of this encounter, Gunawan emphasized the need to recognize that when women, such as myself, actively contribute to raising awareness about this matter, are outspoken in their support for women\u8217 s rights, and resist such actions, it exposes us to a heightened susceptibility to attacks. Indeed, I am fortunate to have grown up in a lifestyle where such concerns do not burden me. While I generally have protection, it is essential to note that this provision is not universally applicable to all women. Indeed, I recognize the need to emphasize and be reminded that many women are endangering their safety by engaging in such actions.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Gunawan's statement emphasizes the inherent dangers encountered by women who openly denounce gender-based violence and champion the cause of women's rights. Although she perceives herself as endowed with a certain degree of safeguarding, she recognizes that numerous other women lack the same privilege and are compelled to jeopardize their safety when they adopt a position on such matters.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 The widely circulated thread shared by Gunawan not only shed light on the subject of deepfake pornography but also exposed the broader issue of sexual assault as a hidden problem with a significantly larger magnitude than what is readily apparent externally. The overwhelming number of direct messages that Gunawan received after her post from individuals recounting their encounters with comparable problems, such as sexual extortion, the unauthorized dissemination of intimate images, or the manipulation of their photos into pornographic material, serves to highlight the pervasive nature of this issue and the absence of fairness for victims.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 The proliferation of deepfake pornography poses a multifaceted problem that is beyond the capacities of current legal structures and law enforcement agencies. The rapid advancement of technology correspondingly increases the possibility of its misuse. This highlights the pressing necessity for more robust and adaptable legal safeguards and a more proactively oriented strategy to prevent and tackle digital sexual abuse. Simultaneously, it also demands more public consciousness and education regarding the hazards of sharing personal photos on the internet. It also emphasizes the necessity of socioeconomic support systems that can offer safeguarding and legal recourse for those affected by deepfake pornography and other manifestations of non-consensual intimate image violence.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 The Impact of Deepfake Pornography on Victims in Indonesia}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24
\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Deepfake pornography is a type of cybercrime classified as the perpetration of sexual violence, namely electronic-based sexual violence in Indonesia. Content manipulation refers to modifying or changing photos or videos to damage the reputation of the individuals portrayed in such materials. In contrast to material produced exclusively for personal use, deepfake pornography is commonly disseminated without the explicit permission of the victim, known as malevolent distribution. This technological exploitation involves the manipulation and distribution of illicit and defamatory content directed against the victim, typically to intimidate or circulate personal photographs or videos. The ramifications for the victims varied, and each person may interpret the impacts uniquely.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 The podcast \u8220 Deepfake Porn and Its Threat to Workers,\u8221  offered by the YouTube channel Progresip Podcast delves into the genuine psychological distress induced by deep fake pornography. Jessica Klein, a certified clinical social worker and adjunct lecturer at the University of Southern California, provided valuable information on the psychological impact endured by victims, indicating that a portion of them display symptoms consistent with PTSD. The symptoms of PTSD may encompass panic episodes, avoidance behavior, melancholy, emotional numbness, feelings of isolation, mistrust, hostility, and substantial disruptions in daily functioning. Klein drew a parallel between the psychological consequences of deepfake pornography and those of actual abuse, underscoring the complete disruption of a victim\u8217 s feeling of safety when their corporeal form is portrayed without their permission and with a large audience.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 The assistant coordinator of the National Commission on Violence Against Women Monitoring Division asserts that the degree of harm experienced by electronic-based sexual violence victims, namely those impacted by deepfake pornography, differs based on the victim's ability to cope with adversity. Nevertheless, victims typically encounter three primary repercussions. Firstly, individuals resort to self-censorship as a result of experiencing shame, which causes them to disengage from both virtual and face-to-face social contacts. Furthermore, psychological consequences emerge, such as PTSD, depression, anxiety disorders, and even suicidal inclinations. Furthermore, victims often experience economic consequences, such as becoming the focus of workplace rumors, being terminated from their jobs because they are seen as a burden to the organization, or facing difficulties in securing work because of the adverse online reputation that follows them. Although electronic-based sexual violence, or Kinetic Somatic Body Eruption, is a type of violence that does not include physical contact between the perpetrator and the victim, any physical effects typically appear after psychological impacts, such as significant hair loss caused by stress, decreased appetite, and substantial weight loss.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 The observed effects are consistent with those reported by Rhadite and Nabillah. Based on interviews with these two informants, it was revealed that victims of electronic-based sexual violence generally experience comparable types of psychological anguish, including social seclusion, financial setbacks, limited movement caused by emotions of humiliation, worry, and diminished self-assurance. Digital technology typically elicits fear and menace among victims, leading them to perceive a lack of safety. Consequently, many individuals opt to cease social media usage completely.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Regarding instances of deepfake pornography or other electronic-based sexual violence-related problems, the adverse consequences not only affect the immediate victims but also extend to their support networks. Indah Gunawan, the administrator of the X account @itsindahg, shared her experiences of feeling inundated by emotional weight. Following the receipt of multiple direct messages from other victims who had similar experiences, she expressed her emotional burden: \u8220 When you receive five or ten direct messages, that is considered insignificant, correct?\u8221  However, it becomes distressing when it accumulates to hundreds of direct messages. Undoubtedly, there is a substantial amount of emotional effort involved in this. I hold great admiration for those who diligently perform the daily task of handling complaints, as it is exceptionally challenging.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Furthermore, Ignatius Rhadite Prastika Bhagaskara, a public lawyer at the Indonesian Legal Aid Foundation-Semarang Legal Aid Institute, shares this viewpoint. Rhadite elucidated that throughout offering victim assistance, there occurs a transmission of adverse energy from the victim to the supporter, which arises from the profound trauma and stress endured by the victim. Consequently, the support staff, who are not directly affected, may experience the development of Secondary Traumatic Stress (STS).}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 B. Hudnall Stamm [49], researchers at a Trauma Center, have documented the adverse consequences that counselors face as a result of their empathic and supporting responsibilities toward trauma clients. Stamm believe that trauma counselors may manifest similar signs of PTSD to their clients. The term secondary denotes the phenomenon where the trauma is directly experienced firsthand by another individual, but the person who observes, assists, or listens to the trauma narrative starts to experience the psychological effects as well.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 The transmission of trauma presents a notable obstacle in assisting victims of deepfake pornography and electronic-based sexual violence, as it underscores the susceptibility of both victims and their support systems to intense emotional suffering. The severe emotional burden imposed on these persons highlights the gravity of the psychological damage attributable to deepfake pornography.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 The urgency of Indonesia\u8217 s Sexual Violence Law: A Legal and Humanitarian Perspective}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj
\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Paragraph (2) of Article 28G in the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia guarantees the right of every individual to be free from torture, harsh treatment, or degrading treatment, as well as the right to seek political asylum from another country [50]. This statement underscores the inherent entitlement of every person to be exempt from the imposition of sexual violence. Prior to the implementation of Law No. 12 of 2022 on Sexual Violence Crimes, a significant number of instances of sexual violence remained unsolved on account of the lack of precise legislation that specifically dealt with the many manifestations of sexual violence [51]. The inadequacies of the Criminal Code in addressing sexual violence led to the failure of many cases to undergo effective legal procedures, therefore depriving victims of their rights and protection, while offenders frequently evaded sufficient punishment.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Despite being a taboo topic in society, sexual violence is seldom reported, resulting in an iceberg phenomenon where the actual numbers greatly surpass the documented incidents. Compiling statistics on violence against women from service providers, hospitals, police, and courts has been the responsibility of the National Commission on Violence Against Women since 2008. The incidence of violence against women surged by an astonishing 792%, almost eight times, between 2008 and 2019. However, this data applies explicitly to female victims, so omitting male victims during sexual violence has the potential to impact individuals of either gender. Nevertheless, it is indisputable that women continue to be the most susceptible demographic to sexual assault [52].}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 The enduring prevalence of sexual violence, even evolving into a pervasive pattern, requires urgent intervention. With technological progress, sexual violence today manifests not just in the physical domain but also in the digital sphere, therefore presenting novel societal risks if not effectively dealt with. Thus, the Law on Sexual Violence Crimes Bill was vigorously advocated as a remedy to public apprehensions, particularly those of victims of sexual assault.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Pancasila, being the }{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 grundnorm}{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2  or essential norm in Indonesia\u8217 s legal system, ought to be applied consistently in every facet of national existence. The endeavor to eradicate sexual assault offenses is a manifestation of the attainment of human fulfillment as embodied in the ideals of Pancasila, namely the second principle, \u8220 just and civilized humanity.\u8221  The humanistic ethics included in this principle encompass acknowledging and treating individuals based on their inherent worth as creations of a supreme deity, acknowledging the equal rights and responsibilities of every human being without any prejudice, and maintaining human ideals [53].}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 The fifth principle, \u8220 social justice for all the people of Indonesia,\u8221  asserts that just treatment is an inherent entitlement for every Indonesian, irrespective of their color, nationality, religion, or gender. This principle encompasses principles of justice, including cultivating a fair disposition towards others and preserving equilibrium between individuals' rights and responsibilities. Within the realm of sexual violence, it is imperative to provide equitable treatment of victims, free from any form of gender-based prejudice. For instance, society and law enforcement frequently engage in unreasonable discrimination against female victims of sexual violence based on factors such as their clothing, relationship with the offender, or other stigmas deeply ingrained in patriarchal culture. However, male victims of sexual violence are frequently left unacknowledged and undervalued due to the prevailing notion that males are invariably motivated by sexual desire, rendering it inconsequential for them to experience hurt from sexual acts perpetrated upon them. It is imperative to eliminate these stigmas as, irrespective of the conditions, a victim remains necessarily a victim. Victims have no reasonable grounds to doubt their entitlement to experience victimization.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Sexual violence, a long-standing issue that has grown increasingly intricate over time, requires acknowledgment and comprehensive understanding. There remains a dearth of consensus in society over the precise definition of sexual violence. Prior to the enactment of the Law on Sexual Violence Crimes, and even somewhat earlier, the prevailing belief in society was that sexual violence solely included acts of rape or sexual activity involving penetration. Diverse manifestations of sexual violence extend beyond just physical contact or penetration.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 The several manifestations of sexual violence can be unequivocally classified as criminal acts in certain circumstances. However, they can also occur within cultural frameworks of society, often seen as customary and not acknowledged as acts of violence. Hence, law enforcement personnel must possess sensitivity in identifying various forms of sexual violence in order to prevent any mistreatment of victims who believe that the treatment they got does not meet the criteria of sexual assault.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 It is important to note that sexual violence is a multifaceted problem that does not always entail penetration. The National Commission on Violence Against Women undertook a 15-year monitoring effort, spanning from 1998 to 2013, to identify various forms of sexual violence. Based on their findings, 15 types of sexual violence were identified, including rape, sexual intimidation, sexual harassment, sexual exploitation, trafficking of women for sexual purposes, forced prostitution, sexual slavery, forced marriage, forced pregnancy, forced abortion, forced contraception and sterilization, sexual torture, inhuman and sexually nuanced punishment, traditional practices with sexual nuances that endanger or discriminate against women, and sexual control, including through discriminatory regulations based on morality and religion [30].}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Despite the identification of numerous forms of sexual assault, it is unfortunate that the current legislation in the Criminal Code concerning sexual violence remains far from comprehensive. Several deficiencies in the Criminal Code give rise to a legal gap in dealing with emerging cases. There exist a minimum of three notable deficiencies in the provisions of the Criminal Code regarding sexual violence. To begin with, the narrow interpretation of rape restricts the offense to situations in which the victim is female and the offender is male, therefore omitting both male victims and female offenders. The restrictive nature of this term is profoundly sexist since rape can take place among men, women, or women and men.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Furthermore, the narrow interpretation of adultery fails to encompass premarital or extramarital sexual encounters between unmarried persons, therefore conflicting with the religious and moral principles prevalent in society. Thirdly, R. Soesilo defines intercourse as the union of male and female genital parts traditionally meant for reproduction, providing a narrow interpretation of the term. However, contemporary sexual behaviors now encompass penetration by the use of tools, objects, or fingers and may also include the anus or mouth.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 The implementation of the Law on Sexual Violence Crimes has dramatically expanded the range of sexual violence, offering much-needed relief to society in the knowledge that the state now safeguards them against different manifestations of sexual violence. Article 4, Paragraph (1) of the Law on Sexual Violence Crimes delineates several manifestations of sexual harassment, encompassing non-physical or physical forms, coerced contraception, coerced sterilization, coerced marriage, sexual torture, sexual exploitation, sexual slavery, and electronic-based sexual assault.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 The incorporation of electronic-based sexual violence into the Law on Sexual Violence Crimes signifies that online sexual abuse has attained a level of severity that necessitates particular focus and legal measures to safeguard victims. Undoubtedly, the increasing prevalence of the internet and social media has correspondingly heightened the possibility of sexual violence. From a constitutional standpoint, the elimination of sexual assault satisfies the constitutional rights of individuals as specified in distinct sections of the 1945 Constitution. The implementation of this directive to safeguard human rights and constitutional rights is also evident in many legislations, including recognized human rights instruments that have been officially adopted into the national legal framework, such as Law No. 39 of 1999 on Human Rights [54].}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Therefore, it is the responsibility of the state to enforce the requirements of the constitution and pass legislation, which includes ensuring safeguards against all types of prejudice and violence, including sexual violence. Sexual violence is antithetical to the nation's ideology and highest legal principles, and it also carries grave repercussions for the victims, social welfare, and the future of the country. Within the framework of electronic-based sexual violence, namely deepfake pornography, the Law on Sexual Violence Crimes has provisioned the \u8220 right to erasure\u8221  or \u8220 right to be forgotten\u8221  for electronic-based sexual violence cases, therefore providing victims the entitlement to have sexually explicit material about their case removed. Incorporating this element demonstrates the extent of constitutional and human rights safeguards, encompassing the physical world and the digital domain.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Right to be Forgotten: A Legal Evolution in Protecting Personal Data}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0
\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 The High Commissioner announced the policy on a \u8220 Victim-Centered Approach\u8221  in December 2020. This policy was in relation to the reaction of the United Nations High Commissioner for Refugees (UNHCR) to violence against women and girls. When it comes to responding to sexual misconduct, this policy emphasizes ensuring the safety, rights, and well-being of victims and survivors and attending to their expressed needs and preferences [55].}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 According to the website of the UNHCR, the victim-centered approach is a method of engaging with victims that emphasizes listening, endeavors to avoid retraumatization, and methodically focuses on the victim\u8217 s safety, rights, well-being, expressed needs, and choices. In addition to ensuring that services are provided in a compassionate and non-judgmental manner, the objective is to give the victim as much control as is humanly possible. Within the framework of the victim-centered approach, the rights and dignity of victims, as well as their well-being and safety, are prioritized. Regardless of the affiliation of the person accused of committing sexual exploitation and abuse, every effort is taken to prevent and treat issues related to these types of crimes.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 According to Benjamin Mendelsohn [56], there are six different types of victims: a completely innocent victim, a victim who has minor guilt, a victim who is equally guilty as the offender, a victim who is more guilty than the offender, a victim who is the only party at fault or who dies as a result of their actions; and an imaginary victim, which occurs in situations where someone claims to be a victim but has not been harmed or lost anything.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Based on the classification presented above, it is possible to conclude that victims of deepfake pornography belong to the first category, which is the category of victims who are entirely innocent. Considering that the pornographic information that was shared is not genuine documentation but rather a distorted result of deepfake technology, this is because the victim did not have any involvement in the case. Further highlighting the fact that victims of deepfake pornography are entitled to special attention and that their rights must be safeguarded is the fact that this has occurred.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 This approach was established in order to gain a better understanding of the position of victims of sexual violence, such as those who have been victims of deepfake pornography, as was discussed earlier. The majority of individuals, when confronted with instances of sexual violence, are overly focused on chasing the perpetrator, and they are ignorant that the victim is the one who requires more care. The destruction of a person\u8217 s good name and dignity due to something that is not their fault occurs when they become a victim of deepfake pornography. The psychological state of the sufferer is significantly impacted as a result of this. The requirements of the victim should be the top priority, and this should be done without diminishing the significance of the appropriate punishments for the offender.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Post-traumatic stress }{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b\i\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ul\cf2 disorder}{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2  (PTSD) is one of the psychological effects that victims of sexual assault, such as deepfake pornography, are subjected to. According to the [57], PTSD is a common psychiatric }{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b\i\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ul\cf2 disorder}{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2  that can result after an individual experiences a traumatic event. PTSD has a broad clinical presentation but is characterized by symptoms impairing cognition, mood, somatic experience, and behavior. PTSD can cause chronic impairments, lead to comorbid psychiatric illness, and lead to an increased risk of suicide.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Whenever a victim is confronted with the debasement of their dignity, mainly when it is founded on slander, the desire to restore their good reputation is naturally the most crucial thing the victim wants to do. In the case of deepfake pornography, the right to erasure, also known as the RtBF, should ideally be among the rights that victims can easily access. If we place excessive emphasis on dealing with the offender, we must ensure that the victim's primary rights are adequately protected.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 As long as the victim\u8217 s bogus pornographic content continues to be shared on the internet, the victim will continue to experience a worsening of the effects and consequences of the situation. In addition, the victim's healing process will be impacted by the victim's experience of being bullied and excluded from society. Therefore, while dealing with incidents of sexual violence, particularly deepfake pornography, it is essential to take the perspective of a victim and give priority to what the victim wants. At the very least, it is possible to assist the victim in recovering and eventually returning to live their life in an ideal condition, provided the victim\u8217 s digital trace is removed from the internet.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 The RtBF is a legal principle that enables persons to effectively seek to delete personal information about previous events from public availability on the internet [58]. This right was initially introduced as a fundamental entitlement within the European Union, allowing individuals to delete their data from internet sites. The inception of RtBF may be attributed to the significant legal case concerning Google Spain SL, Google Inc. v. Agencia Espa\'f1ola de Protecci\'f3n de Datos (AEPD) and Mario Costeja Gonz\'e1lez in 2014. Gonz\'e1lez initiated legal proceedings to invalidate a story published by La Vanguardia, a Spanish newspaper, and formally demanded that Google Spain and Google Inc. eliminate any hyperlinks to this article from their search results. Gonz\'e1lez contended that the material had become irrelevant since the matter had been settled [59].}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 The European Court of Justice ultimately found in favor of Gonz\'e1lez, therefore defining fundamental precepts for the RtBF. If processing an individual\u8217 s data by search engines infringes against their fundamental rights, the court ruled that the search engines cannot justify processing the data on the grounds of legitimate interests, such as profit. Individuals are entitled to demand the deletion of connections to third-party websites that include personal information if the information is found to be incorrect, insufficient, no longer pertinent, or excessive. Nevertheless, this entitlement is not without limitations; if the material is considered essential for the benefit of the general public, such as in situations involving prominent individuals, the search engine has the authority to keep the material.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 This case established a significant legal principle as it was the initial instance where the RtBF was examined and implemented in a practical situation. Despite its existence for more than four decades, the notion was officially integrated into European law on April 27, 2016, with the enactment of Regulation 2016/679, commonly referred to as the General Data Protection Regulation. Following a two-year transition window, the General Data Protection Regulation becomes effective on May 25, 2018. A key objective of the General Data Protection Regulation is to safeguard individuals\u8217  essential rights to their personal data in the digital age and to encourage conscientious and open data utilization. Article 6 of the General Data Protection Regulation delineates particular legal foundations for processing personal data, including \u8220 Consent\u8221 . Personal data processing is typically forbidden unless allowed by law or with the data subject\u8217 s explicit consent.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 The right to erasure or RtBF refers to an individual\u8217 s entitlement to request the deletion of their data in situations when it is processed and disseminated on the internet without their proper consent. By Article 17 of the General Data Protection Regulation, individuals who are data subjects are entitled to immediately request the removal of personal data related to them. Conversely, data controllers are required to erase the data promptly under specific circumstances. These criteria encompass the data becoming unnecessary for its original purpose, the revocation of consent, illegal processing, and the requirement to adhere to legal responsibilities.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 The RtBF was initially implemented under Article 26 of the Electronic Information and Transactions Law in Indonesia. While not expressly disclosed, the article acknowledges that any electronic information about personal data must be utilized with the explicit permission of the subject in question. Suppose an individual\u8217 s rights are infringed upon. In that case, they can initiate legal proceedings to obtain reparation, and operators of electronic systems are obligated to remove all pertinent material within their jurisdiction upon receiving a court order.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Nevertheless, the rule exhibits ambiguity, as it needs precise instructions on implementing the RtBF. Government Regulation No. 71 of 2019, intended to give specific rules for executing the RtBF under the Electronic Information and Transactions Law, likewise needs clear guidance. The rule mandates that operators of electronic systems must promptly remove electronic information or documents under their authority upon request. However, a precise definition of the scope of the right to erasure is needed.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 The RtBF is recognized in both the Sexual Violence Law and the Personal Data Protection Law. Article 70 of the Law on Sexual Violence Crimes confers upon victims of electronic-based sexual abuse the entitlement to have sexually explicit material pertaining to them deleted, therefore indirectly embodying the RtBF. Article 8 of the Personal Data Protection Law confers to data subjects the entitlement to terminate their data's processing, erasure, and destruction in compliance with legal provisions. However, the absence of legislative measures presents difficulty in upholding these rights and guaranteeing sufficient safeguarding for victims in various areas.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Legal and Societal Challenges in Addressing Deepfake Pornography in Indonesia: The Implementation of the Right to be Forgotten}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum
\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 The increasing number of sexual violence cases over time underscores the critical role played by service providers in assisting victims. These organizations, including the National Commission on Violence Against Women, AwasKBGO, and the Semarang Legal Aid Institute, have been actively involved in providing support, particularly for victims of technology-facilitated sexual violence, such as deepfake pornography. Through interviews with various representatives from these organizations, this article delves into the dynamics of victim support, the challenges involved, and the broader efforts to uphold the RtBF for victims.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 According to Fadillah, a member of the National Commission on Violence Against Women, the process of handling all forms of electronic-based sexual violence shares similar patterns because the medium is the same\u8212 the internet. One of the most significant difficulties in handling such cases is identifying the perpetrators, as many individuals are often involved in the process, from the creators and editors of the content to those responsible for its distribution. This layered involvement makes it particularly challenging to track down and hold accountable all the actors behind a deepfake pornography incident.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 As an organization working within the scope of these cases, Fadillah shared that the National Commission on Violence Against Women tailors its assistance to the specific needs of each victim. Some victims come forward simply to share their experiences and relieve their anxieties, while others seek psychological or legal support. When psychological assistance is needed, the National Commission on Violence Against Women directs victims to government-provided services such as the Integrated Service Centers for the Empowerment of Women and Children and the Women\u8217 s Empowerment and Child Protection Agency. This referral process reflects the National Commission on Violence Against Women's stance on the importance of involving the state in addressing cases of sexual violence to ensure that victims receive comprehensive protection.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 For legal assistance, the National Commission on Violence Against Women refers victims to state institutions that facilitate legal aid or to Legal Aid Organizations that provide pro bono support. In cases of technology-facilitated sexual violence, such as deepfake pornography, the National Commission on Violence Against Women also recommends that victims seek digital security consultations. These consultations typically involve discussions on the nature of the problem, the victim\u8217 s use of social media, potential threats, and interim measures for safety. These consultations are often facilitated by organizations such as SafeNet or the cyber-based violence taskforce, both of which specialize in digital security and online gender-based violence.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 The support provided by the National Commission on Violence Against Women does not end with these referrals. Suppose victims encounter obstacles in their pursuit of justice, such as when a case is reported to the police and categorized under pornography law, which may portray the victim as a subject of pornography. In that case, the National Commission on Violence Against Women offers further assistance. The organization provides legal opinions to the police to clarify the legal standing of the victim and the nature of the case. Additionally, the National Commission on Violence Against Women can act as an expert witness in court if necessary, testifying to support the victim's claims.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Fadillah also highlighted that even before the enactment of the Sexual Violence Crime Law, the National Commission on Violence Against Women had already been advocating for the RtBF for victims of technology-based sexual exploitation. Prior to the introduction of this law, the National Commission on Violence Against Women worked with the Ministry of Communication and Information Technology to request the removal of content validated as electronic-based sexual violence. This collaboration arose out of a lack of legal regulations at the time, prompting the National Commission on Violence Against Women to push for state involvement in protecting victims. In these cases, the Ministry of Communication and Information Technology removed the content from digital platforms. During this period, the state initiated the process of content removal, requesting online platforms to take down flagged content.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Following the enactment of the Law on Sexual Violence Crimes, the state is now required to take a more proactive role in handling such cases. This begins with the police, who must recognize that the content is under investigation and freeze access to it, preventing the public from viewing it. Only law enforcement officials, such as the police and prosecutors, may access the content during this stage. If it is later proven that the content constitutes electronic-based sexual violence, it can be permanently removed from digital platforms. The prosecutor includes the content in their charges, allowing the court to rule on its removal, after which the Ministry of Communication and Information Technology takes it down based on the court\u8217 s decision.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 AwasKBGO, an initiative of SAFEnet, focuses on tackling cyber-based violence. SafeNet, a civil society organization based in Denpasar, Bali, advocates for digital rights, including the right to access the internet, freedom of expression, and security in the digital space. AwasKBGO offers a range of services, including public education through informative content and scientific research on electronic-based sexual violence, aiming to raise awareness and improve public understanding of these issues. The organization also provides consultations on digital privacy and security, helping individuals learn how to protect their privacy and security in the digital space to avoid becoming victims of electronic-based sexual violence.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 In addition to these consultations, AwasKBGO assists victims in reporting electronic-based sexual violence content to digital platforms, which often serve as the sites where the content is circulated. Although the final decision on removing the content lies with the platform, AwasKBGO ensures that victims' reports are handled effectively. Nabillah, a representative from AwasKBGO, shared that the organization provides psychosocial support, assists in reporting accounts, and escalates takedown requests to digital platforms. However, Nabillah also noted that electronic-based sexual violence content, once disseminated online, cannot be entirely erased, as it can be replicated in various ways, such as through screenshots.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 In a recent interview with Nabillah, she described how AwasKBGO and its network are currently supporting a victim of deepfake pornography, a journalist whose photo was manipulated into pornographic content and shared on a platform. The case is being pursued through legal channels, with the victim receiving assistance from a coalition of civil society organizations, including SAFEnet. However, Nabillah acknowledged the case's complexity, as it intersects with the victim's professional life, which is further complicated by the policies of the company the victim works for.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Rhadite, a public lawyer with Semarang Legal Aid Institute, reflected on the difficulties of supporting victims of electronic-based sexual violence both before and after the enactment of the Sexual Violence Crime Law. Before the law was passed, Rhadite and his colleagues faced significant challenges, especially during the COVID-19 pandemic, when the increased use of digital spaces led to a rise in electronic-based sexual violence cases. At that time, no comprehensive legal instruments were used to protect victims' rights or provide a clear path to justice. Additionally, there were no channels for victim advocates or legal representatives to seek state intervention in addressing the harms suffered by victims. As a result, much of the support provided relied on the solidarity of civil society, with advocates organizing safe houses, referring victims for psychological support, and providing legal assistance to the best of their ability.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 While the passage of The Law on Sexual Violence Crimes was expected to resolve many of these issues, Rhadite explained that new challenges have emerged. With the law's introduction, the number of complaints has skyrocketed as victims feel more empowered to come forward, knowing they have legal protection. However, the lack of implementing regulations for the law has hindered its practical application, leaving many victims without the full support they had hoped for. In handling electronic-based sexual violence cases, Semarang Legal Aid Institute has pursued legal action, often starting with cease-and-desist letters that demand the perpetrator stop their actions, remove any posts containing sexual content of the victim, delete stored content, and issue a public apology. When these demands are ignored, Semarang Legal Aid Institute escalates the case, threatening further legal action, often prompting the perpetrator to comply.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Regarding the RtBF in deepfake pornography cases, Rhadite pointed out that victims can exercise this right independently through mechanisms like StopNCII.org. StopNCII.org is a project run by the Revenge Porn Helpline that employs innovative technology to help prevent the spread of intimate images. The project has partnered with major social media platforms, including Facebook, TikTok, Reddit, Instagram, and even pornography websites like Pornhub, to help victims regain control of their content.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 However, one might wonder about the role of the courts in determining whether content can be removed independently. The answer lies in the victim's needs and the specific circumstances of each case. Fadillah from the National Commission on Violence Against Women noted that while the RtBF is vital for victim recovery, there are instances where victims feel that the perpetrator must be held accountable, especially if they hold a position of power. In such cases, litigation may be necessary to ensure justice is served and the perpetrator is punished. Ultimately, the legal process aims to restore a sense of normalcy for the victim, even if it cannot entirely undo the harm caused.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 New legal and societal difficulties have arisen all over the world, including in Indonesia, as a result of the proliferation of deepfake pornography, which is a distressing expression of non-consensual intimate images and violent abuse. As a result of their photographs being modified and spread without their consent, victims of this type of digital sexual exploitation are frequently left with memories of traumatic experiences. These challenges have progressed beyond individual transgressions to become a systemic societal problem due to the rapid advancement of AI technologies, such as tools for creating deep fakes. There is a potential legal remedy available to victims of deepfake pornography in Indonesia under the RtBF, even though this remedy is laden with difficulties in terms of its actual use.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 RtBF is a legal principle that was derived from the General Data Protection Regulation of the European Union. Its purpose is to allow individuals to seek the removal of personal information from the internet in situations when it is no longer relevant or where it was given without authorization. In Indonesia, the RTBF is recognized by Article 26 of the Electronic Information and Transactions Law, which permits the deletion of documents or information irrelevant to electronic systems. On the other hand, the substantive and procedural components of implementing RtBF continue to be underdeveloped and challenging to implement, particularly in cases involving deepfake pornography.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 The judicial system in Indonesia has been criticized on numerous occasions for its slow response to new and growing kinds of criminal activity, particularly those that include technology. The Indonesian legal system is frequently delayed in addressing the societal repercussions of globalization and technology advancements, as Rhadite, a social analyst and advocate, pointed out in an interview. Rhadite\u8217 s comments about the Philippines were made. He cites examples such as the late adoption of the Electronic Information and Transactions Law in 2008, even though cybercrimes had been expected for years, and the passage of the Sexual Assault Act only in 2022, even though there has been a sustained public outcry for legal protections against sexual assault.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 For example, deepfake pornography is a type of criminal activity that has not yet been subjected to complete legal scrutiny in Indonesia. When it comes to the unique nature of AI-related abuses such as deepfake pornography, there is still a glaring void in the law, even though the Law on Sexual Violence Crimes and other legislation, such as the Personal Data Protection Law and the Criminal Code can provide some protection to victims. In situations when their rights have been violated, victims have few options available to them since the rapid development of artificial intelligence technology has surpassed the ability of the legal system to respond adequately.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 In a perfect world, RtBF would offer victims of deepfake pornography the opportunity to remove content that has been modified off the internet and safeguard their privacy all at the same time. However, more than the legislative structure that is now in place in Indonesia is needed to allow for the accelerated and all-encompassing implementation of this right. Even though Article 26 of the Electronic Information and Transactions Law offers a legal foundation for removing damaging or irrelevant digital content, the application of this provision has been problematic due to the ambiguous definition of what constitutes \u8220 irrelevant\u8221  information. In addition, the regulations being implemented per Government Regulation No. 71 of 2019 need to provide specific instructions on how to put RtBF into effect. This means that a significant portion of the procedure is left to the discretion of government officials and online platforms.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 When it comes to the deployment of RtBF, deepfake pornographic scenarios provide their own set of distinct issues. The modification of photographs or films in order to produce sexually explicit content that gives the impression of being honest but is not, in fact, real constitutes not only an invasion of the victim\u8217 s right to privacy but also a direct assault on the victim's dignity. As a result of the widespread dissemination of their modified photographs on the internet, victims frequently find themselves powerless, and removing these images becomes a Herculean undertaking.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 As part of its efforts to protect victims of sexual assault, the Law on Sexual Violence Crimes includes provisions that are specifically designed to protect victims of sexual exploitation that are assisted by technology. The right of victims to have harmful content deleted from digital platforms is guaranteed by Article 70 of the law, which is by the principles of RtBF. On the other hand, the Law on Sexual Violence Crimes has not been able to function effectively in practice because there are no regulations in place to implement it. When attempting to have the content removed, victims frequently encounter insurmountable bureaucratic obstacles. Furthermore, because there is no clear legal framework in place, many requests for content deletion have not been responded to.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 In addition, the RtBF rules included in Indonesia\u8217 s legal system are not commonly recognized or well-publicized, especially among those who work in the legal field and those who deal with law enforcement. Consequently, victims of deepfake pornography might not be aware of their rights, or they might encounter resistance from online platforms that are slow to respond to removal requests. Both of these outcomes are possible. In addition, the lack of public understanding about RtBF, in conjunction with the limited efforts made by the government to popularize the concept, has further impeded its potential as a solution for victims of sexual abuse transmitted through digital platforms.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 When examining the efficiency of RtBF in Indonesia, the theory of legal systems developed by Lawrence Meir Friedman [23] provides a helpful lens through which to assess the situation. According to Friedman, substantive law, legal structure, and legal culture are the three components that make up a legal system. These components are interconnected and affect one another. In order for RtBF to be successfully implemented for victims of deep fake pornography, all three components must operate synchronized with one another.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 In terms of substantive legislation, Indonesia has made headway by passing laws such as the Law on Sexual Violence Crimes and the Personal Data Protection Law, which are designed to protect victims of digital sexual exploitation in theory. Nevertheless, as Alia, a legal researcher, pointed out, these rules primarily concentrate on concerns that occur further down the chain, such as prosecuting those who commit crimes and compensating those who are victimized. Although these steps are significant, they do not address the issue that lies further upstream: the regulation of artificial intelligence systems themselves.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Currently, Indonesia has no comprehensive legislation that oversees the right way to use artificial intelligence. Despite the fact that the government has produced soft rules, such as the 2020\u8211 2045 National Strategy for Artificial Intelligence, these papers are not legally binding. They are not adequate for tackling the complexities of AI-driven crimes such as deepfake pornography. The gendered impact of artificial intelligence technology is frequently overlooked by these techniques, particularly in the manner in which these technologies can be weaponized against women through the use of deepfake pornography.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 One of the most critical aspects of implementing RtBF is the legal framework, which refers to the institutions accountable for enforcing the law. Regrettably, Indonesian law enforcement organizations have been criticized for their insufficient handling of instances involving sexual assaults that occur online. In many cases, victims of deepfake pornography are met with reactions from the authorities that are either delayed or dismissive. The police may lack the technological ability or sensitivity to address the issue effectively. In conversations with victims, it has been noted that the police frequently shift responsibility back to the victim, asking them to submit proof or investigate the matter themselves. This adds to the emotional weight that victims already endure, which is already a significant strain.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 The separation of responsibility within law enforcement is another factor that makes the situation even more problematic. Cases that involve sexual violence are often reported to the Women and Children\u8217 s Protection Unit, even though the Cybercrime Directorate is responsible for managing investigations into crimes that occur online. On the other hand, the Women and Children\u8217 s Protection Unit frequently does not possess the resources or knowledge required to deal with cybercrimes, resulting in an uncoordinated and underperforming response.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 The final factor that plays a significant part in determining how RtBF is implemented is legal culture, which may be defined as the attitudes, values, and beliefs associated with the administration of justice. When it comes to digital sexual violence, the culture of rape and deeply rooted patriarchal attitudes in Indonesia frequently contribute to the trivialization of the issue. Those who are victims of deepfake pornography are usually exposed to victim-blaming, with many people in society feeling that women who publish images of themselves online are \u8220 asking for it\u8221  in some way. The victims may feel embarrassed or disbelieved when they report the crime, which makes it difficult for them to seek justice. This cultural backdrop makes it difficult for victims to seek justice.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 The case of Anya Cahyara, a content producer who fell victim to deepfake pornography, is a striking illustration of how the culture of rape operates in Indonesia. Anya did not receive support; instead, she was confronted with charges that she was responsible for her victimization. These accusations were based on the fact that she uploaded images of herself online or how she dressed. The practice of blaming victims in this manner not only discourages additional victims from coming forward but also perpetuates the notion that women\u8217 s bodies are public property that may be exploited and twisted at will.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 There are a few essential actions that need to be completed in order to implement RtBF in Indonesia successfully. The first step is for the government to make the development of a complete legal framework a top priority. This framework should expressly address the use of artificial intelligence and the potential damages that it can create, including deepfake pornography. Both upstream regulations that govern the ethical use of artificial intelligence and downstream protections for victims of digital crimes should be included in this framework.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Second, the police and other law enforcement organizations need to be better prepared to deal with cases of sexual assaults that occur online. Officers will receive training on gender sensitivity and digital forensics as part of this initiative. Additionally, the Cybercrime Directorate and the Public Protection Agency will work to improve their coordination. The victims of deepfake pornography should not be allowed to traverse the legal system on their own; they require law enforcement that is both helpful and aggressive, and that places a priority on their well-being.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Finally, there is a need for a cultural revolution in order to demolish the culture of rape and to fight patriarchal beliefs that normalize violence against women. Campaigns to raise public awareness about RtBF and digital sexual assault should be intensified, and efforts should be made to educate the public about the dangers of deepfake pornography and the significance of providing support to victims.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Conclusion}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 The emergence of deepfake pornography in Indonesia presents a significant concern, particularly for women, as it exacerbates the challenges of online sexual exploitation. The accessibility of AI technology has led to the extensive production and dissemination of altered sexual content, with platforms such as Telegram playing a significant role in its widespread distribution. This phenomenon has significantly altered the landscape of online sexual exploitation cases, eliminating the necessity for perpetrators to have direct access to their victims. Individuals affected experience significant repercussions, such as mental health challenges, social disconnection, and financial setbacks. Organizations such as the National Commission on Violence Against Women, AwasKBGO, and Semarang Legal Aid Institute offer psychological, legal, and digital security support; however, challenges remain due to inadequate law enforcement and insufficient victim-centred policies.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Law enforcement agencies face challenges in implementing the correct legal framework, frequently depending on the Electronic Information and Transactions Law, which inadequately safeguards victims\u8217  privacy. Cultural factors, such as patriarchal norms and the prevalence of rape culture, impede the pursuit of justice by perpetuating the objectification of women and sidelining victims. To effectively tackle this issue, it is essential to adopt a multifaceted strategy that encompasses legal reform, enhanced training for law enforcement, and increased public awareness, all aimed at guaranteeing justice and protection for victims.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
